or><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURAI MASAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ODA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAISHI HIDEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARAYAMA, HIROTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATSUHIRA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWABATA, YOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURAI, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ODA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAISHI, HIDEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Fused-heterocycle dicarboxylic diamide derivatives represented by general formula (I); and herbicides containing the derivatives as the active ingredient, wherein R&lt;1&gt; is H or (C1-C6)alkyl; R&lt;2&gt; and R&lt;3&gt; are each H, (halo)(C1-C6)alkyl, (C3-C8)cycloalkyl, substituted amino(C1-C6)alkyl, (substituted) phenyl(C1-C6)alkyl, (substituted) phenyl(C1-C6)alkoxy or the like, or R&lt;2&gt; and R&lt;3&gt; are united to form a 5- or 6-membered heterocycle bearing at least one member selected from among O, S and N; X is H, halogeno, NO2, CN, (C1-C6)alkyl, (substituted) phenyl, (substituted) phenoxy or the like; and (II) is or the like (wherein Y, R&lt;4&gt; and R&lt;9&gt; are each H, halogeno, NO2, CN, (C1-C6)alkyl or the like; and A, B, D, E, F, G, J and K are each O, S, N, sulfinyl or the like).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des dérivés de diamide dicarboxylique à hétérocycle condensé représentés par la formule générale (I); et des herbicides contenant les dérivés comme principe actif. Dans la formule (I), R&lt;1&gt; est H ou alkyle en C1-C6; R&lt;2&gt; et R&lt;3&gt; sont chacun H, (halo)alkyle en C1-C6, cycloalkyle en C3-C8, aminoalkyle en C1-C6 substitué, phénylalkyle en C1-C6 (substitué), phénylalcoxy en C1-C6 (substitué) ou analogue, ou R&lt;2&gt; et R&lt;3&gt; sont réunis de manière à former un hétérocycle à 5 ou 6 chaînons portant au moins un élément sélectionné dans le groupe comprenant O, S et N; X est H, halogéno, NO2, CN, alkyle en C1-C6, phényle (substitué), phénoxy (substitué) ou analogue; et (II) est (III) ou analogue (Y, R&lt;4&gt; et R&lt;9&gt; étant chacun H, halogéno, NO2, CN, alkyle en C1-C6 ou analogue; et A, B, D, E, F, G, J et K sont chacun O, S, N, sulfinyle ou analogue).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>